  "description": "#5098 — group titles order by UTF-8 BYTES, as `cmp_group`'s `str` compare does, not by the UTF-16 code units JS `<` compares. The two spellings DISAGREE on this seed and only on a pair like it: 'ｱ' half-width katakana (U+FF71, EF BD B1) and '🍎' red apple (U+1F34E, F0 9F 8D 8E). Bytes rank the katakana first (EF < F0); code units rank the apple first, because its leading surrogate D83C is below FF71. The mock's `compareSortKeys` used JS `<` and served the apple group first. Pages are seeded apple-first so the code-unit answer is also the insertion order, and a handler that dropped the sort entirely reddens too. The titleless half of the same comparator is not reachable from here — a fixture seed's content is `unwrap_or(\"\")`, so no seed can make `blocks.content` NULL; it is pinned in `conformance-query-backlink-groups.test.ts`.",
